
========================================================================
  PART 1: THE FULL TOURNAPLEX f-VECTOR
========================================================================

  f_k = number of (k+1)-vertex tournaments = 2^{C(k+1, 2)}

  f_0 = 2^C(1,2) = 2^0 = 1
  f_1 = 2^C(2,2) = 2^1 = 2
  f_2 = 2^C(3,2) = 2^3 = 8
  f_3 = 2^C(4,2) = 2^6 = 64
  f_4 = 2^C(5,2) = 2^10 = 1024
  f_5 = 2^C(6,2) = 2^15 = 32768
  f_6 = 2^C(7,2) = 2^21 = 2097152
  f_7 = 2^C(8,2) = 2^28 = 268435456
  f_8 = 2^C(9,2) = 2^36 = 68719476736
  f_9 = 2^C(10,2) = 2^45 = 35184372088832

  f-vector: [1, 2, 8, 64, 1024, 32768, 2097152, 268435456, 68719476736, 35184372088832]
  This is 2^{0, 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21, 28, 36, 45} = 2^{C(k+1,2)}
  The exponents are the TRIANGULAR NUMBERS!

  Euler characteristic (truncated at k=9):
  chi = sum (-1)^k f_k = -35115918982201
  Partial sums:
    K=1: chi = 1
    K=2: chi = -1
    K=3: chi = 7
    K=4: chi = -57
    K=5: chi = 967
    K=6: chi = -31801
    K=7: chi = 2065351
    K=8: chi = -266370105
    K=9: chi = 68453106631

========================================================================
  PART 2: TRANSITIVE TOURNAPLEX
========================================================================

  T_trans: only transitive tournaments (no 3-cycles).
  A transitive tournament on n vertices = a total order on [n].
  f_k = number of transitive tournaments on k+1 vertices = (k+1)!

  f-vector: [1, 2, 6, 24, 120, 720, 5040, 40320, 362880]
  = [1!, 2!, 3!, 4!, 5!, 6!, 7!, 8!, 9!]
  = [1, 2, 6, 24, 120, 720, 5040, 40320, 362880]

