    K=2: chi = -1
    K=3: chi = 5
    K=4: chi = -19
    K=5: chi = 101
    K=6: chi = -619
    K=7: chi = 4421
    K=8: chi = -35899

  Note: sum_{k=0}^{n} (-1)^k (k+1)! is related to SUBFACTORIALS!
  D_n = n! sum_{k=0}^n (-1)^k / k! = subfactorial (derangements)
  Our sum: sum (-1)^k (k+1)! = ???
    K=1: sum = 1
    K=2: sum = -1
    K=3: sum = 5
    K=4: sum = -19
    K=5: sum = 101
    K=6: sum = -619
    K=7: sum = 4421
    K=8: sum = -35899
    K=9: sum = 326981

